  {
   "title": "Plurals: mga and plural adjectives",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Tagalog follows a **plurality rule**: either the subject or the predicate may be made plural, and making **both** plural is optional."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In **Sina Helen at Tom ay mga batà**, the article **sina** shows that the subject is plural, and **mga** before batà shows that the noun is plural. **Mga** is a plural marker with **no meaning on its own**. It is pronounced **ma-nga**."
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "Plural adjectives"
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Adjectives form their plural by **duplicating the first syllable of the root word**. The root of **mabaít** (kind) is **baít**, so the plural is **mababaít**."
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "The plural recipe",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Singular",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "ma",
         "r": "other"
        },
        {
         "t": "baít",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Plural",
