 "recap": [
  "Si (one person) and siná (two or more persons) go before names of persons.",
  "Ang (one) and ang mga (two or more) go before things and places. A place always takes ang.",
  "Basic sentence: article + subject + ay + predicate.",
  "Mga is said ma-nga and has no meaning on its own.",
  "Plural adjectives duplicate the first syllable of the root: mabaít, mababaít.",
  "Either the subject or the predicate may be plural; making both plural is optional."
 ]
